{"toolCallId":"call_48529084e1024c929c232622d20a84f7","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"== REQ ==\n101:| REQ-011 | With `--quiet`, every warning the script writes to stderr is still written to stderr: `--quiet` trims stdout only and never suppresses, redirects or closes stderr. |\n== TASK ==\n57:- [ ] T015 Keep the quiet branch stdout-only so REQ-011 holds: it returns before the report echoes and leaves fd 2 untouched, so every warning the script writes to stderr still reaches stderr under `--quiet` (`$S`, run after T007). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 2>\"$P/scratch/stderr-default.txt\" >/dev/null` then `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc 50 --files 2 2>\"$P/scratch/stderr-quiet.txt\" >/dev/null` then `diff \"$P/scratch/stderr-default.txt\" \"$P/scratch/stderr-quiet.txt\"` prints nothing.\n== AC ==\n66:| AC-011 | REQ-011 | Given the same valid input, When one run uses `--quiet` and the other does not, Then the two stderr streams are identical, so `--quiet` trims stdout only and any warning still reaches stderr | `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 2>scratch/stderr-default.txt >/dev/null` and `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc 50 --files 2 2>scratch/stderr-quiet.txt >/dev/null` then `diff scratch/stderr-default.txt scratch/stderr-quiet.txt` prints nothing | Unmet | - |\n== counts ==\n11\n12\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"903a76","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
